                <pb facs="0537" n="223" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg223"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/115</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-08">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">September 8, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>87. Your August 28, 11 a.m. British Government has decided to adhere to the
                    Declaration of London, subject to certain modifications and additions. These are
                    explained in the following memoranda and order in council of the British
                    Government:</p>
                <p>[Here follow memoranda 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 and British order in council quoted from
                    telegram No. 483 from London, undated.]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d372-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>This Government is giving the proposed additions and modifications its attentive
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
